<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arame of Urartu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 860–840 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arame was the first known king of Urartu, ruling in the mid-ninth century BCE. He is known only from Assyrian sources: the annals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> record campaigns against him from 859 BCE and the sack of his royal city <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arzashkun">Arzashkun</a> in 856 BCE. Armenian tradition later remembered a hero named Aram, sometimes linked with him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arame-of-urartu.jpg" alt="Arame of Urartu" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urartu860-840.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
